  "user_intent": {
    "original": "Use the Read tool to read each of these five files, one Read call per file: private/deny.txt, private/deny (1).txt, private/John's notes.txt, private/a,b.txt and private/k=v.txt. Then tell me exactly what the Read tool returned for each one, quoting any error message word for word.",
    "evolution": [
      "Use the Bash tool to run each of these commands exactly as written, one Bash call per command (do not combine them), and then reply with one line per command giving only its exit status:\nls\nls src\nls docs\ncat src/mod1.py\ncat src/mod2.py\ncat src/mod3.py\ncat src/mod4.py\ngrep -n TODO src/mod5.py\ngrep -n TODO src/mod6.py\ngrep -c PLOVER docs/design.md",
      "Use the Bash tool to run each of these commands exactly as written, one Bash call per command (do not combine them), and then reply with one line per command giving only its exit status:\ncat docs/plan.md\ncat docs/faq.md\nwc -l docs/glossary.md\ngit log --oneline\ngit diff HEAD~1 --stat\ncd \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/sessc space/proj\" && git status --short\nls -l \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/sessc space/proj/src\"\nhead -n 1 src/mod7.py\nhead -n 1 src/mod8.py\ngrep -rn \"def f\" src",
      "Use the Bash tool to run each of these commands exactly as written, one Bash call per command (do not combine them), and then reply with one line per command giving only its exit status:\nls -l private/\nwc -c \"private/deny (1).txt\"\nls -l private/a,b.txt private/k=v.txt\ngit log --oneline -- \"private/John's notes.txt\"\nwc -c \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/sessc space/proj/private/deny.txt\"\necho \"checked private/deny.txt and John's notes.txt\"\nls private/*.txt\ngit log --oneline -- private/k=v.txt",
      "Use the Read tool to read each of these files, one Read call per file: README.md, src/mod1.py, src/mod2.py, src/mod5.py, src/mod8.py, docs/design.md, docs/glossary.md. Then reply with just the word done.",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__recall once for each of these queries, one call per query: \"PLOVER-3\", \"TODO tune\", \"path:src/mod4.py\", \"path:private/deny.txt\", \"path:private/John's notes.txt\", \"path:private/*.txt\", \"cache warms\". Then call mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__re_read with path \"src/mod1.py\", re_read with path \"docs/plan.md\", re_read with path \"private/a,b.txt\" and re_read with path \"private/deny (1).txt\". Reply with one line per call: the call, and count/denied for recall or found/denied for re_read.",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__timeline with no arguments, then mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__already_tried with target \"src/mod1.py\" and approach \"inline f1\", then mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with hash of the README.md capture if you know it (otherwise skip it). Reply in one short line per call."
    ]
  },
